_meanings:
A kind of yogic meditation or samādhi in which the
 object of meditation remains distinct, though the mind is absorbed in its
 contemplation; as opposed to the {#asaMprajYAta#} variety in which the
 distinction between knowledge and its object is completely obliterated;
 ({#DyeyaDyAtfBAvayuktasAkAraDyAnasamADiH saMprajYAtaH saMvitsaMvedyavilopena#}
 {#nirAkArasvaprakASaparamAnandalakzaRAtmasAmrAjyaDyAnasamADirasaMprajYAtaH iti#}

 {#yogaSAstram#}); {#ityudIrya sa hariM prati saMprajYAtavAsitatamaH samapAdi#} <ls>N. 21. 119</ls>.
